Pious - Empowered/Warded/Buffs
    {"name":"soul covenant","req":"pious 1","tags":"","effect":"Make a pact, oath, or pledge to a powerful entity. (A god, demon, dragon, eldritch being, etc.) Work with your GM to create this covenant. For example, a god may ask you to 'Protect the forest.', or a demon may want you to 'Sacrifice a soul every day!'. Should you fail to keep your covenant you may lose access to this Trait.\nPick any Art of Tier 3 or less (regardless of if you have the Architype). Once per Rest, you can offer something to your Patron to activate this Art without spending Strain. For example, a god may ask for a prayer, or a demon may ask for blood.","extra":""},
    {"name":"soul bound relic","req":"pious 1","tags":"","effect":"At the end of a Rest you may bind a small item to your soul. While a creature is holding or wearing the Relic you may cast spells that target only them (or items they are carrying) as if you were able to touch them or be 1 tile away from them.","extra":""},
    {"name":"boon infusion","req":"pious 1","tags":"","effect":"When you spend Strain to activate a non-Attack Art you may spend 1 Strain to give the affected target(s) Warded or Empowered for up to 1 hour. This bonus is given after the Art's effects.","extra":""},
    {"name":"soul blade","req":"pious 1","tags":"","effect":"Turn a Melee Weapon you wield into your Soul Weapon. This weapon does damage equal to 1+SOUL or if it's two handed 3+SOUL, has Returning, can Glow, and cannot be broken except by Arts.","extra":""},
    
    {"name":"soul tempo","req":"pious 2","tags":"","effect":"When you spend 3 or more Strain in a turn gain Empowered until the end of your next turn (~20 seconds).","extra":""},
    Missing - wep? sup? ooc? religion?
    
    {"name":"powered alignment","req":"pious 3","tags":"","effect":"While you are Empowered, you have +1 Speed and +1 on Weapon Attack Sums.\nWhile you are Warded, you refund 1 Strain at the end of your turn and may give Glow on targets you touch or hit.","extra":""},
    {"name":"boon's protection","req":"pious 3","tags":"","effect":"Once per turn, you may turn Warded into Empowered or Empowered into Warded. They keep their origional duration.","extra":""},
    
    {"name":"power from within","req":"pious 4","tags":"","effect":"Arts you or an ally activate that affect just you or items you wield, cost 1 less Strain, to a minimum of 1.","extra":""},
    {"name":"purified soul","req":"pious 4","tags":"","effect":"When you die, instead you turn into a Spirit. While as a Spirit you have the Undead tag, have half health, are permanently Slowed, +1 Dodge against non-Art Attacks, can move through non-metal walls, and cannot carry or use items. If you die as a Spirit you cannot be resurrected. When your body is resurrected you must be present or it will fail.","extra":""},
    


    
Spirits - Arts/OOC/Summons
    {"name":"curse","req":"spirits 1","tags":"","effect":"At the end of a Break or Rest you may give a Curse to a creature that you have a part of (hair, nails, skin, etc.). This Curse gives -1 to a Stat (non-stacking), -1d6 on CHARM rolls against you, have a rain cloud above them constantly making them Wet, or you can create your own curse no stronger than these options. The curse ends when they are blessed, you die, they die, or by an effect that removes magic.","extra":""},
    {"name":"hex","req":"spirits 1","tags":"","effect":"When you activate a targeted non-Focus Art you may Focus on the Art for up to 1 minute, save any dice spent. At the beginning of your turn you may re-activate the Art on the same target with the same dice sum by spending half the Art's Strain cost (rounded up, to a minimum of 1).","extra":""},
    {"name":"death's eyes","req":"spirits 1","tags":"","effect":"While your eyes are closed or you are Blind you can see wisps of the dead. At the end of a Rest these wisps give you +1d4 on your choice of specific Check until your next Rest. (Some examples are, animal handling, religion, or deciphering text.)","extra":""},
    missing
    
    {"name":"grave research","req":"spirits 2","tags":"","effect":"All your created or summoned Followers may gain the Monstrosity or Undead tag. When you create or summon a Monstrosity or Undead you may spend 1 Strain to have them gain one of the following bonuses: Bloody, Ghostly, or Decaying.\n- **Bloody:**  They can move through spaces 1 tile smaller than themselves and gain +1 on Grapple rolls.\n- **Ghostly:** They gain the 'Spirit Walk' Art and their Attacks do Essence damage instead of their default type. \n- **Decaying:** They take -1 damage from Physical and Essence damage, but have -1 Speed. (Minimum of 1 for damage and Speed.)","extra":""},
    {"name":"blood sacrifice","req":"spirits 2","tags":"","effect":"When you do an Attack you may spend 2 Health (ignores Shielding) to increase any damage by 1d4.","extra":""},
    
    {"name":"group practice","req":"spirits 3","tags":"","effect":"When you Focus on an Art that targets ally or yourself you may give the Art's effects to an additional creature. (That creature must be a valid target for the Art.)","extra":""},
    {"name":"???","req":"spirits 3","tags":"","effect":"At the end of a Rest you may create a Mount Follower. Describe your Mount and how you created it. This Mount has 3xSOUL Max Health, 9 Speed, 0 in all other stats, the Construct, Monstrosity, or Undead tag, and one of the following bonuses (this can be changed at the end of a Rest):\n- The Mount can Fly and Hover\n- The Mount can move through non-metal walls (taking its rider with it) but has 6 Speed (instead of 9).\n- The Mount is Resistant to Physical, and Elemental damage.","extra":""},
    
    {"name":"necromancer","req":"spirits 4","tags":"","effect":"Followers you create or summon have +1 damage while they are within 6 tiles of you, and your Undead Followers can be healed by your Traits and Arts (Not by a Medkit or Bandage).","extra":""},
    missing


    
Arcanist - Arts/Control/Basic
    {"name":"art token","req":"arcanist 1","tags":"","effect":"You may spend Strain to activate an Art you know, turning the activation into a Token of your choosing. Later a creature can spend ### destroying the Token to activate the imbued Art without spending Strain. You may have up to ARCANA number of Tokens at a time.","extra":""},
    {"name":"art manipulator","req":"arcanist 1","tags":"","effect":"When you activate an Art you may spend 1 Strain then pick 1 of the following:\n- The Arts effects happen at a later time based on a specific trigger.\n- An Art requires 1 less dice to cast. Use a 3 for the missing dice value.\n- An Art activates without any noticeable movement or sounds.","extra":""},
    {"name":"flexible repertoire","req":"arcanist 1","tags":"","effect":"At the end of a Rest you may swap one of your Arts for a different Art.","extra":""},
    {"name":"familiar","req":"arcanist 1","tags":"","effect":"At the end of a Rest create a Familiar Follower. The Familiar has 2xLEVEL Max Health and Strain, +1 Dodge, 7 Speed, 1 in a Main-Stat (Body, Mind, or Soul), 2 in one Sub-Stat of your choice, and 0 for all other Stats. They know the Art 'telepathy' and have a Spectral Attack ('Mage Gauntlets'), You may pick its type (Animal, Construct, Monstrosity, Planar, or Undead), two Tier 1 Arts of your choice (it needs the stat in order to take an Art), and appearance each time it is created.\n- When you gain a stat increase the Familiar gains +1 in a Sub-Stat of your choice. You may only ever have 1 Familiar at a time, if you were to create a Familiar while one already exists the first one morphs into the new one.\n\nThe familiar improves as you do gaining the following benefits when you hit certain Tiers.\n- *Tier 2* - You may pick one Tier 2 Art of your choice for the Familiar.\n- *Tier 3* - Choose one (you cannot change this choice later). The Familiar can Fly, gain 1 Art you know, or gain +1 to a Main Stat.\n- *Tier 4* - You may pick three Tier 1 Arts and two Tier 2 Arts of your choice for the Familiar.","extra":""},

    {"name":"magical knowledge","req":"arcanist 2","tags":"","effect":"You learn 2 additional Arts of your choice that you meet the requirements for.","extra":""},
    {"name":"art augmenter","req":"arcanist 2","tags":"","effect":"When you activate an Art you may spend 2 Strain then pick 1 of the following:\n- An Art with Range has its range doubled. Art's with a range of Touch have Reaching 2.\n- Change any Statuses given by an Art to either 2 Burn, Wet, Marked, Charmed, 1 Stun, Warded, or Empowered. It lasts for the same duration as the original Status (or until end of turn).\n- Arts that deal damage do an additional 2 damage.","extra":""},
    
    {"name":"signature art","req":"arcanist 3","tags":"","effect":"When you take this Trait choose an Art you know. You may activate that Art up to your SOUL times per Break or Rest without spending Strain.\nYou cannot change this chosen Art except through extremely powerful sources, and if you remove this Art from your known Arts you cannot use this Trait.","extra":""},
    {"name":"art ???","req":"arcanist 3","tags":"","effect":"When you activate an Art you may spend 3 Strain then pick 1 of the following:\n- Non-area Arts can have a second target. (Focusing on both effects if needed)\n- Arts with an area can be compressed to give a target the effect 3 times (rolling dodge/contests 3 times).\n- When you activate an Art that has an area effect, you may choose any number of targets that are not affected by the Art.","extra":""},
    
    {"name":"stacking arts","req":"arcanist 4","tags":"","effect":"When you activate an Art you may activate a different Art with the same triggers or conditions on the same target without spending more dice (you still spend Strain). For instance you may activate the Arts 'Cleave' and 'Smite' on the same Weapon Attack.","extra":""},
    {"name":"imbuement","req":"arcanist 4","tags":"","effect":"At the end of a Rest you may imbue a non-Attack Art you know into a target. The target then has the Art's effect active on them until your next Rest. This Art does not cost Strain or Dice, does not require Focus, has a duration lasting until your next Rest, and can be re-activated ARCANA times per Rest on the target without spending Dice or Strain.","extra":""},
    
    




Face? - Control/OOC/Buffs/Debuffs
    {"name":"show, don't tell","req":"charm 1","tags":"","effect":"Whenever you speak or do a performance you can subtly add a message into it. You may target any number of creatures you can see to learn the message. Then the creature(s), and only the creature(s), will learn your message regardless of distance.","extra":""},
    {"name":"???","req":"charm 1","tags":"","effect":"Up to CHARM times per Rest, you may give a creature that can see or hear you +1d4 on a Check or Contest.","extra":""},
    {"name":"i know a guy","req":"charm 1","tags":"","effect":"When you are in a jam, describe someone your character would know. Give them a name, say how you think they could be useful, and choose one fact from below:\n- They owe me a favor, but they'll be hard to find. \n- They're going to ask for something in exchange. \n- They're always in a great deal of trouble. \n- We used to be together. It's a long story. \n- We didn't part on great terms.","extra":""},
